     *Variable Scope*     Global,         
                          Session         
     *Dynamic Variable*   Yes             
                          *Permitted        
                          Values*         
     *Type*               `boolean'        
     *Default*            `1'             

     This variable controls whether updates to a view can be made when
     the view does not contain all columns of the primary key defined
     in the underlying table, if the update statement contains a
     `LIMIT' clause. (Such updates often are generated by GUI tools.)
     An update is an *Note `UPDATE': update. or *Note `DELETE': delete.
     statement. Primary key here means a `PRIMARY KEY', or a `UNIQUE'
     index in which no column can contain `NULL'.

     The variable can have two values:

        * `1' or `YES': Issue a warning only (not an error message).
          This is the default value.

        * `0' or `NO': Prohibit the update.

