Aliases for column names in *Note `CREATE VIEW': create-view.
statements are checked against the maximum column length of 64
characters (not the maximum alias length of 256 characters).

Identifiers are stored using Unicode (UTF-8). This applies to
identifiers in table definitions that are stored in `.frm' files and to
identifiers stored in the grant tables in the `mysql' database. The
sizes of the identifier string columns in the grant tables are measured
in characters. You can use multi-byte characters without reducing the
number of characters permitted for values stored in these columns,
something not true prior to MySQL 4.1. As indicated earlier, the
permissible Unicode characters are those in the Basic Multilingual
Plane (BMP). Supplementary characters are not permitted.


