11.8 Using Data Types from Other Database Engines
=================================================

To facilitate the use of code written for SQL implementations from
other vendors, MySQL maps data types as shown in the following table.
These mappings make it easier to import table definitions from other
database systems into MySQL.

This table provides a mapping of MySQL data types to data types from
other vendors.

Other Vendor Type         MySQL Type
*Note `BOOL':             *Note `TINYINT': integer-types.
integer-types.            
*Note `BOOLEAN':          *Note `TINYINT': integer-types.
integer-types.            
`CHARACTER VARYING(M)'    `VARCHAR(M)'
*Note `FIXED':            *Note `DECIMAL': fixed-point-types.
fixed-point-types.        
*Note `FLOAT4':           *Note `FLOAT': floating-point-types.
floating-point-types.     
*Note `FLOAT8':           *Note `DOUBLE': floating-point-types.
floating-point-types.     
*Note `INT1':             *Note `TINYINT': integer-types.
integer-types.            
*Note `INT2':             *Note `SMALLINT': integer-types.
integer-types.            
