13.1.9 `ALTER VIEW' Syntax
--------------------------

     ALTER
         [ALGORITHM = {UNDEFINED | MERGE | TEMPTABLE}]
         [DEFINER = { USER | CURRENT_USER }]
         [SQL SECURITY { DEFINER | INVOKER }]
         VIEW VIEW_NAME [(COLUMN_LIST)]
         AS SELECT_STATEMENT
         [WITH [CASCADED | LOCAL] CHECK OPTION]

This statement changes the definition of a view, which must exist.  The
syntax is similar to that for *Note `CREATE VIEW': create-view. and the
effect is the same as for *Note `CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW': create-view.
See *Note create-view::. This statement requires the `CREATE VIEW' and
`DROP' privileges for the view, and some privilege for each column
referred to in the *Note `SELECT': select. statement.  *Note `ALTER
VIEW': alter-view. is permitted only to the definer or users with the
`SUPER' privilege.


