13.7.1 Account Management Statements
------------------------------------

* Menu:

* create-user::                  `CREATE USER' Syntax
* drop-user::                    `DROP USER' Syntax
* grant::                        `GRANT' Syntax
* rename-user::                  `RENAME USER' Syntax
* revoke::                       `REVOKE' Syntax
* set-password::                 `SET PASSWORD' Syntax

MySQL account information is stored in the tables of the `mysql'
database. This database and the access control system are discussed
extensively in *Note server-administration::, which you should consult
for additional details.

*Important*:

Some releases of MySQL introduce changes to the structure of the grant
tables to add new privileges or features. Whenever you update to a new
version of MySQL, you should update your grant tables to make sure that
they have the current structure so that you can take advantage of any
new capabilities. See *Note mysql-upgrade::.


