     Whether *Note `InnoDB': innodb-storage-engine. performs change
     buffering, an optimization that delays write operations to
     secondary indexes so that the I/O operations can be performed
     sequentially. The permitted values are `inserts' (buffer insert
     operations), `deletes' (buffer delete operations; strictly
     speaking, the writes that mark index records for later deletion
