   * `sync_binlog'

     Options for sync_binlog

     *Command-Line        `--sync-binlog=#'        
     Format*                              
     *Option-File Format* `sync_binlog'        
     *System Variable     `sync_binlog'        
     Name*                                
     *Variable Scope*     Global          
     *Dynamic Variable*   Yes             
                          *Permitted        
                          Values*         
     *Platform Bit Size*  `32'            
     *Type*               `numeric'        
     *Default*            `0'             
     *Range*              `0 ..           
                          4294967295'        
                          *Permitted        
                          Values*         
     *Platform Bit Size*  `64'            
     *Type*               `numeric'        
     *Default*            `0'             
     *Range*              `0 ..           
                          18446744073709547520'        

     If the value of this variable is greater than 0, the MySQL server
     synchronizes its binary log to disk (using `fdatasync()') after
     every `sync_binlog' writes to the binary log. There is one write
