14.4.13.1 Performance Patches from Google
.........................................

Oracle gratefully acknowledges the following contributions from Google,
Inc. to improve InnoDB performance:

   * Replacing InnoDB's use of Pthreads mutexes with calls to GCC
     atomic builtins, as discussed in *Note
     innodb-performance-latching::. This change means that InnoDB mutex
     and and rw-lock operations take less CPU time, and improves
     throughput on those platforms where the atomic operations are
     available.

   * Controlling master thread `I/O' rate, as discussed in *Note
     innodb-performance-thread_io_rate::. The master thread in InnoDB
     is a thread that performs various tasks in the background.
     Historically, InnoDB has used a hard coded value as the total
     `I/O' capacity of the server. With this change, user can control
     the number of `I/O' operations that can be performed per second
     based on their own workload.

