     binary log's contents from time to time as for any other file. A
     value of 1 is the safest choice because in the event of a crash
     you lose at most one statement or transaction from the binary log.
     However, it is also the slowest choice (unless the disk has a
     battery-backed cache, which makes synchronization very fast).


