     *Note `mysqld': mysqld.  since the last time it was restarted.

     For more information, see *Note
     mysql-cluster-replication-conflict-resolution::.

   *  `Ndb_conflict_fn_epoch'

     Used in MySQL Cluster Replication conflict resolution, this
     variable shows the number of rows found to be in conflict using
     `NDB$EPOCH()' conflict resolution on a given *Note `mysqld':
     mysqld. since the last time it was restarted.

     For more information, see *Note
     mysql-cluster-replication-conflict-resolution::.

