22.3.16 Known Issues and Limitations
------------------------------------

The following are some known issues and limitations for MySQL
Connector/J:

   * When Connector/J retrieves timestamps for a daylight saving time
     (DST) switch day using the `getTimeStamp()' method on the result
     set, some of the returned values might be wrong. The errors can be
     avoided by using the following connection options when connecting
     to a database:

                  useTimezone=true
                  useLegacyDatetimeCode=false
                  serverTimezone=UTC


