22.5 MySQL Connector/C
======================

* Menu:

* connector-c-versions::         MySQL Connector/C Versions
* connector-c-platforms::        MySQL Connector/C Supported Platforms
* connector-c-contents::         MySQL Connector/C Distribution Contents
* connector-c-installation::     Installing MySQL Connector/C
* connector-c-applications::     Building MySQL Connector/C Applications

MySQL Connector/C is a client library that implements the C API for
client/server communication. It is a standalone replacement for the
MySQL client library shipped with MySQL Server distributions. See *Note
c-api-implementations::.

Reasons to use MySQL Connector/C:

   * If you need only the client library, MySQL Connector/C provides
     everything required. There is no need to compile or install the
     MySQL Server package, which is much larger.

   * MySQL Connector/C does not rely on the MySQL Server release cycle.
     Bug fixes and new features can be distributed independently of
     MySQL Server releases.

For documentation of the C API implemented by MySQL Connector/C, see
*Note c-api::.

For release notes detailing the changes in each release of MySQL
Connector/C, see MySQL Connector/C Release Notes
(http://dev.mysql.com/doc/relnotes/connector-c/en/).

The following discussion covers these topics:

   * MySQL Connector/C versions and supported platforms

   * MySQL Connector/C distribution contents

   * Obtaining and installing MySQL Connector/C

   * Building client programs that use MySQL Connector/C


