22.6.8.84 Class `constants.FieldType'
.....................................

This class provides all supported MySQL field or data types. They can
be useful when dealing with raw data or defining your own converters.
The field type is stored with every cursor in the description for each
column.

The following example shows how to print the name of the data type for
each column in a result set.

     from __future__ import print_function
     import mysql.connector
     from mysql.connector import FieldType

     cnx = mysql.connector.connect(user='scott', database='test')
     cursor = cnx.cursor()

     cursor.execute(
       "SELECT DATE(NOW()) AS `c1`, TIME(NOW()) AS `c2`, "
       "NOW() AS `c3`, 'a string' AS `c4`, 42 AS `c5`")
     rows = cursor.fetchall()

     for desc in cursor.description:
       colname = desc[0]
       coltype = desc[1]
       print("Column {} has type {}".format(
         colname, FieldType.get_info(coltype)))

     cursor.close()
     cnx.close()

The `FieldType' class cannot be instantiated.


