22.8.7.11 `mysql_drop_db()'
...........................

`int mysql_drop_db(MYSQL *mysql, const char *db)'

* Description *

Drops the database named by the `db' parameter.

This function is deprecated. It is preferable to use *Note
`mysql_query()': mysql-query. to issue an SQL *Note `DROP DATABASE':
drop-database. statement instead.

* Return Values *

Zero if the database was dropped successfully. Nonzero if an error
occurred.

* Errors *

   * `CR_COMMANDS_OUT_OF_SYNC'

     Commands were executed in an improper order.

   * `CR_SERVER_GONE_ERROR'

     The MySQL server has gone away.

   * `CR_SERVER_LOST'

     The connection to the server was lost during the query.

   * `CR_UNKNOWN_ERROR'

     An unknown error occurred.

* Example *

     if(mysql_drop_db(&mysql, "my_database"))
       fprintf(stderr, "Failed to drop the database: Error: %s\n",
               mysql_error(&mysql));


