File: manual.info,  Node: apis-php-book.mysqlnd-qc,  Next: apis-php-book.mysqlnd-uh,  Prev: apis-php-book.mysqlnd-ms,  Up: apis-php

22.9.3 Mysqlnd query result cache plugin (`mysqlnd_qc')
-------------------------------------------------------

* Menu:

* apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.key-features::  Key Features
* apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.limitations::  Limitations
* apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.name::     On the name
* apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.quickstart::  Quickstart and Examples
* apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.setup::    Installing/Configuring
* apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.constants::  Predefined Constants
* apis-php-ref.mysqlnd-qc::      mysqlnd_qc Functions
* apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.changes::  Change History

Copyright 1997-2012 the PHP Documentation Group.

The mysqlnd query result cache plugin adds easy to use client-side
query caching to all PHP MySQL extensions using See section
"apis-php-mysqli" in the online manual.

As of version PHP 5.3.3 the MySQL native driver for PHP ( `mysqlnd')
features an internal plugin C API. C plugins, such as the query cache
plugin, can extend the functionality of See section "apis-php-mysqli"
in the online manual.

Mysqlnd plugins such as the query cache plugin operate transparent from
a user perspective. The cache plugin supports all PHP applications and
all PHP MySQL extensions ( mysqli, mysql, See section
"apis-php-ref.pdo-mysql" in the online manual). It does not change
existing APIs.

No significant application changes are required to cache a query.  The
cache has two operation modes. It will either cache all queries (not
recommended) or only those queries marked with a certain SQL hint
(recommended).


File: manual.info,  Node: apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.key-features,  Next: apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.limitations,  Prev: apis-php-book.mysqlnd-qc,  Up: apis-php-book.mysqlnd-qc

22.9.3.1 Key Features
.....................

Copyright 1997-2012 the PHP Documentation Group.

   * Transparent and therefore easy to use

        * supports all PHP MySQL extensions

        * no API changes

        * very little application changes required

   * Flexible invalidation strategy

        * Time-to-Live (TTL)

        * user-defined

   * Storage with different scope and life-span

        * Default (Hash, process memory)

        * APC (http://www.php.net/ref.apc)

        * MEMCACHE

        * sqlite

        * user-defined

   * Built-in slam defense to prevent cache stampeding.


File: manual.info,  Node: apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.limitations,  Next: apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.name,  Prev: apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.key-features,  Up: apis-php-book.mysqlnd-qc

22.9.3.2 Limitations
....................

Copyright 1997-2012 the PHP Documentation Group.

The current 1.0.1 release of PECL mysqlnd_qc does not support PHP 5.4.
Version 1.1.0-alpha lifts this limitation.

Prepared statements and unbuffered queries are fully supported.  Thus,
the plugin is capable of caching all statements issued with `mysqli' or
`PDO_MySQL', which are the only two PHP MySQL APIs to offer prepared
statement support.


File: manual.info,  Node: apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.name,  Next: apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.quickstart,  Prev: apis-php-mysqlnd-qc.limitations,  Up: apis-php-book.mysqlnd-qc

22.9.3.3 On the name
....................

Copyright 1997-2012 the PHP Documentation Group.

The shortcut `mysqlnd_qc' stands for `mysqlnd query cache plugin'. The
name was chosen for a quick-and-dirty proof-of-concept. In the
beginning the developers did not expect to continue using the code base.
Sometimes PECL/mysqlnd_qc has also been called `client-side query
result set cache'.


