22.9.4 Mysqlnd user handler plugin (`mysqlnd_uh')
-------------------------------------------------

* Menu:

* apis-php-mysqlnd-uh.security::  Security considerations
* apis-php-mysqlnd-uh.docs-note::  Documentation note
* apis-php-mysqlnd-uh.name::     On the name
* apis-php-mysqlnd-uh.quickstart::  Quickstart and Examples
* apis-php-mysqlnd-uh.setup::    Installing/Configuring
* apis-php-mysqlnd-uh.constants::  Predefined Constants
* apis-php-class.mysqlnduhconnection::  The MysqlndUhConnection class (`MysqlndUhConnection')
* apis-php-class.mysqlnduhpreparedstatement::  The MysqlndUhPreparedStatement class (`MysqlndUhPreparedStatement')
* apis-php-ref.mysqlnd-uh::      Mysqlnd_uh Functions
* apis-php-mysqlnd-uh.changes::  Change History

Copyright 1997-2012 the PHP Documentation Group.

The mysqlnd user handler plugin (`mysqlnd_uh') allows users to set
hooks for most internal calls of the MySQL native driver for PHP (`See
section "apis-php-mysqli" in the online manual').  Mysqlnd and its
plugins, including PECL/mysqlnd_uh, operate on a layer beneath the PHP
MySQL extensions. A mysqlnd plugin can be considered as a proxy between
the PHP MySQL extensions and the MySQL server as part of the PHP
executable on the client-side. Because the plugins operates on their
own layer below the PHP MySQL extensions, they can monitor and change
application actions without requiring application changes. If the PHP
MySQL extensions (mysqli, mysql, See section "apis-php-ref.pdo-mysql"
in the online manual) are compiled to use `mysqlnd' this can be used
for:

   * Monitoring

        * Queries executed by any of the PHP MySQL extensions

        * Prepared statements executing by any of the PHP MySQL
          extensions

   * Auditing

        * Detection of database usage

        * SQL injection protection using black and white lists

   * Assorted

        * Load Balancing connections

The MySQL native driver for PHP (See section "apis-php-mysqli" in the
online manual) features an internal plugin C API. C plugins, such as
the mysqlnd user handler plugin, can extend the functionality of See
section "apis-php-mysqli" in the online manual. PECL/mysqlnd_uh makes
parts of the internal plugin C API available to the PHP user for plugin
development with PHP.

*Status*:

The mysqlnd user handler plugin is in alpha status. Take appropriate
care before using it in production environments.


File: manual.info,  Node: apis-php-mysqlnd-uh.security,  Next: apis-php-mysqlnd-uh.docs-note,  Prev: apis-php-book.mysqlnd-uh,  Up: apis-php-book.mysqlnd-uh

22.9.4.1 Security considerations
................................

Copyright 1997-2012 the PHP Documentation Group.

PECL/mysqlnd_uh gives users access to MySQL user names, MySQL password
used by any of the PHP MySQL extensions to connect to MySQL. It allows
monitoring of all queries and prepared statements exposing the
statement string to the user. Therefore, the extension should be
installed with care. The `PHP_INI_SYSTEM' configuration setting
`mysqlnd_uh.enable' can be used to prevent users from hooking mysqlnd
calls.

Code obfuscators and similar technologies are not suitable to prevent
monitoring of mysqlnd library activities if PECL/mysqlnd_uh is made
available and the user can install a proxy, for example, using
auto_prepend_file (http://www.php.net/ini.auto-prepend-file).


